      "concern": "The Definition instructs calling alg-cauchy-matvec-at-roots-of-unity on the root grid, then says, “The root $-1$ is handled directly and is never included in this Cauchy evaluation.” The called algorithm evaluates all M roots and has no excluded-root input. For even M it therefore also evaluates the auxiliary Cauchy sums at −1. Those evaluations are harmless: lem-s4-convolution-root-of-unity-reduction, Proof 1.2, proves that no mapped nonexceptional pole equals −1. The instructions should distinguish discarding that auxiliary output from excluding the root from the called routine.",
